      "exampleEnglish": "The weather is hot in summer.",
      "grammarNote": "الطَّقْسُ ('the weather') is almost always definite with ال, even though it's talking about weather in general, not one specific known thing — similar to how الْخُبْزَ meant bread in general back in level 25. حَارّ and بَارِد are ordinary adjectives, agreeing the normal way you learned in level 4 — no special pattern like the أَفْعَل colors or comparatives.",
